Subject: [PATCH] Scripted walks out of the taller picture after turns, or
 round what's in the way (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the field at the DS's pixel size, a scripted walk that ends past the
DS's top or bottom but inside the taller picture was made longer only
when it went straight up or down. Now:

- A walk whose last steps go up or down, after other steps (Dawn leaving
  Sandgem Town after the tour: a step south, 5 west, 10 north; Dawn
  leaving Jubilife after the Galactic battle: a step east, 9 south;
  Looker's way out of Jubilife), is made longer the same way.
- Where the way on is not clear (Dawn's 10 steps north out of Sandgem end
  under a row of trees), the walker goes round, after the script's walk:
  on that way first, else east, else west, until it is out of the taller
  picture or beside the wider one.
- A walk that is blocked by a wall where the DS's picture ended, with a
  door in reach (Dawn leaving the lab beside the player), first tries a
  step that way, then across to the door's column, then straight on to
  the door: down the middle of the room. The search for a way to the
  door is the fallback, as before.
- SetPosition forgets what the wider screen did to a walker's walk, so
  someone the script puts somewhere afterwards (Looker, put in the road
  for later) isn't moved back again when the script ends.

